WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.700
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week on
Teen Wolf they paid off the young Derek plot

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.910
and teased the Benefactor, the main villain
of season 4.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.280
There were a few funny moments, but the Kate
Were-Jaguar story turned out to be something

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.669
way sneakier.

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:17.840
Before we get started Hello to any new people
who are just finding me, I'm doing weekly

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.599
Teen Wolf videos.

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:20.849
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:24.340
I'm also going to try and do bonus videos
too.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:32.200
I was really glad they resolved the big mystery
of young derek in episode 1, but because the

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.020
real story was something totally different
we need to spend most of our time talking

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.070
about that.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.920
So what I'm going to do is Top 5 Moments,
then a quick breakdown of the new character

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.860
they introduced and what he's going to be
doing this season and then an overall review

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:46.860
of the episode.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.240
Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the
episode yet, but here we go.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.640
Number 5 - Malia Meets Peter

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.870
So in case you missed it last season, Malia
is Peter's biological daughter, her mother

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.160
was Mrs Tate, married to Mr Tate.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.430
Her mother had an affair with Peter, but she
was raised as Mr Tate's daughter.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.780
Everyone thought she died, but then during
season 3 she appeared after living as a coyote

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:08.790
for years.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.990
Cut to now where she's completely failing
at history class in the most adorable way

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.350
possible.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.590
Her meeting Peter was huge, Peter knew exactly
who she was but she doesn't know he's her

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.590
father.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:25.870
Remember earlier in the episode Scott told
Stiles that telling the truth was always the

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.720
best way to go.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:33.340
Them not telling Malia about Peter will probably
bite them in the ass later this season, literally.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.399
Malia would totally bite someone.

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:41.270
I also caught some Peter vibes coming off
Malia, she's got a lot of his rage and impulsiveness.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:46.260
Peter is a little more subtle just having
the benefit of years of experience but I can

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.960
totally see his subconscious presence in her.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.610
Not like when he was controlling Lydia, but
shades of him behind her eyes.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:58.381
I wonder if that means there's a high likelihood
she'll betray the pack for Peter when she

00:01:58.381 --> 00:01:59.549
learns the truth.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:06.679
I think Stiles is her anchor, so if she were
ever forced to choose I think the outcome

00:02:06.679 --> 00:02:12.250
would depend on where their relationship is
and what he does to win her back.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.780
Doesn't it kind of seem like anyone associated
with the Hale family gets tied up in a betrayal

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.380
plot sooner or later.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:22.370
Even Derek who was BFFs with Scott during
season 3 had been an antagonist before that.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.240
Definitely a high probability of Malia flip
flopping sides back and forth this year.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.750
Number 4 - Kate Wants To Control Her Shifting

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.290
It was a little confusing, Kate was being
manipulated just like she was manipulating

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.500
Young Derek.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.410
She really did want the Triskelion so she
could control her shifting.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.070
And Yes, I do think she'll listen to Peter's
advice and figure it out on her own eventually.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:45.751
It's been a while since I've seen the triskelion
symbol too so whenever Peter called it out

00:02:45.751 --> 00:02:49.500
I actually thought of the Triskelion on Marvel's
Agents of SHIELD.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:54.102
It's a giant base that doubles as prison for
supervillains in the Marvel Universe.

00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:57.760
The Hale Family's Triskelion means a bunch
of different things, usually each time it

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.720
shows up like in season 1, season 2 and season
3.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.510
It's a metaphor for something different.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.020
In greek and celtic mythology it represents
the stages of life, like birth, life, death

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.440
and the stages of the moon.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.960
New, half and Full.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.480
In this episode I think for Derek and Kate
it represents Past, Present and Future because

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.420
of their previous relationship and Derek's
physical transformation.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.240
But for Peter and Malia I think it represented
Mother, Father, Daughter.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.080
It's all about progression, family and relationships.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:31.870
Which is what a lot of this episode teased.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:35.750
Number 3 - Lydia's Powers Start To Manifest
More

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:39.240
So Lydia spacing out into Banshee mode and
finding the murder scene is going to keep

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.880
happening until she learns to control her
powers.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.570
Just like Kate is trying to learn to control
her shifts.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.263
I like to think they're on the same path,
learning to control their demon powers, even

00:03:46.263 --> 00:03:48.410
though Kate is a were jaguar I'm just going
to think of her as a demon.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.670
A really nasty one.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.370
I like that they used the cell phone pictures
for comedy.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.590
It wouldn't be Lydia if they didn't try to
make if funny.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:59.150
I feel like her comedic powers exist in a
direct relationship with her proximity to

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.150
Stiles.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.700
The closer they drift together, the funnier
she gets.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.760
I can't imagine how sticky that bathroom was
after they filmed that scene.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.120
In some of the trailers we saw scenes of Lydia
investigating murders, this goes into the

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.630
idea of the Benefactor and the Deadpool List
which I'll explain in a second.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.130
But there's going to be a lot of serial killings
going on.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.049
For Lydia it will be like moth to flame.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:23.419
So until she learns to control her power,
in each new episode she's going to space out

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:24.900
and just show up at random dead bodies.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.729
I like that they used a bathroom for this
first big kill.

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:32.629
I kind of thought it was a callback to the
bathroom in episode 1, the one Kate refused

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:39.460
to kill

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.099
Number 2 - Young Derek Transformers Back to
Regular Derek

00:04:43.099 --> 00:04:47.300
This was another logic jump the show was asking
you to make, but remember he was transforming

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.550
back while he was going apeshit on the berserkers.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.830
Who knew young derek was so good at krav maga
and parkour?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.830
This was all happening while Peter was explaining
how to use anger to control the shift.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:02.249
It made me think that young Derek just tapped
into his primal rage and that's what caused

00:05:02.249 --> 00:05:03.930
him to revert back to normal.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:06.803
The only issue I had with this was they didn't
do a great job of explaining the mechanics

00:05:06.803 --> 00:05:08.259
of young Derek.

00:05:08.259 --> 00:05:11.340
Like what kind of a spell did Kate use to
make his body and mind revert to a younger

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.509
state and if a young Derek could transform
into old Derek using raw emotion, how come

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:19.410
Old Derek can't do the same thing in reverse.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.900
Feel free to write your theory about the time
travel magic in the comments.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:26.580
But I think Stiles dad making the silly timey
wimey explanation was a note to us the viewers

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.949
from the writers saying, don't poke too many
holes in this.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:32.599
And my Number 1 Moment - The Benefactor Appears
and Reveals The True Plan

00:05:32.599 --> 00:05:36.120
It's a bit of a deus ex machina, but that
person at the end is The Benefactor.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.580
He's the main villain this season and the
one who used Kate to get to the Bearer Bonds.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.750
All kinds of questions here but I have a few
theories about why he took the money.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.819
Creator Jeff Davis was talking about the idea
of the Deadpool list in season 4.

00:05:49.819 --> 00:05:53.759
A kill list of all the supernatural creatures
living in Beacon Hills.

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:57.379
The Benefactor is behind it or will be behind
it and I think he's going to use those Bearer

00:05:57.379 --> 00:05:58.650
Bonds to finance the kills.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.939
He has to pay out when someone kills a name
on the list.

00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:03.050
So presumably, a hunter could make a shit
load of money by killing a bunch of werewolves,

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.150
kanima or anything else living in the area.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.699
Joseph Gatt is the actor listed as playing
the Benefactor.

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:11.040
In case you didn't see it, he played a warg
on Game of Thrones Season 4.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.790
You can't tell from this picture, but he's
super huge.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.949
Like as big as one of the berserkers.

00:06:15.949 --> 00:06:19.969
It's unclear why the Benefactor character
wants all the supernatural creatures dead,

00:06:19.969 --> 00:06:24.219
but we can eliminate some familiar faces from
being responsible, like Peter.

00:06:24.219 --> 00:06:27.410
It's seemed like he genuinely flipped out
when his money was stolen.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:32.279
But wouldn't it be crazy if this was like
Usual Suspects and he was the Verbal Kint,

00:06:32.279 --> 00:06:37.559
the Kevin Spacey character that secretly turns
out to be Kaiser Sose.

00:06:37.559 --> 00:06:40.840
I don't think that's what's going on, but
I like the idea that Peter is the Loki of

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.120
the series, always the trickster.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:45.759
You can never trust your eyes or ears when
he's around.

00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:48.729
He's always working some long con to regain
his alpha status.

00:06:48.729 --> 00:06:51.389
Remember, his eyes still glow blue, not Alpha
Red.

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:56.220
So let me know what your favorite moment was
and why do you think the Benefactor wants

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.069
to kill all supernatural creatures in Beacon
Hills.

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:02.780
And will it cause a mega alliance to form.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.990
There's a lot more than just werewolves living
there.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:10.909
Here's a couple important things that didn't
make it into my top 5, but that are important.

00:07:10.909 --> 00:07:11.909
The pairings.

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:15.300
I liked the way they mixed and matched characters
from last episode.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.190
Last week it was Kira and Malia, this week
we saw Kira go off with Lydia.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:22.159
I really like the way pairing people brings
unexpected energy.

00:07:22.159 --> 00:07:26.930
Like when Malia went off with Scott and Peter
had what was probably the funniest line in

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.270
the episode "We're not exactly a brain trust
of geniuses here".

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:34.229
You wouldn't get that if they always paired
Scott with Stiles because Stiles is the genius.

00:07:34.229 --> 00:07:38.189
I'm really looking forward to more Malia Peter
scenes, we still need to see Stiles and Kira

00:07:38.189 --> 00:07:41.331
get some moments and Malia and Lydia, actually
I take it all back, Malia and Lydia is who

00:07:41.331 --> 00:07:42.749
I want to see together next.

00:07:42.749 --> 00:07:45.599
They can go all Scooby Doo on one of Lydia's
murder scenes.

00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:49.770
The Kira Scott relationship is probably going
to take the longest to get anywhere but I

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.139
think it will.

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:55.779
Malia and Stiles are definitely a thing and
Stiles and Lydia are like the sexless old

00:07:55.779 --> 00:07:57.389
couple that just crack jokes.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:08:01.789
Or like buddy cops that have an unconsummated
relationship.

00:08:01.789 --> 00:08:04.690
Stiles and Lydia would make for a great True
Detective Season 2

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:08.479
And Malia is now my new favorite character.

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:12.539
She's got all of the right qualities to kick
butt while getting herself into hilarious

00:08:12.539 --> 00:08:16.210
situations and stay adorable while she's making
a mess of things.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:18.029
Like history class.

00:08:18.029 --> 00:08:19.029
She's like a puppy.

00:08:19.029 --> 00:08:20.759
You can't get mad at a puppy.

00:08:20.759 --> 00:08:24.009
Scott is still on the path to becoming a leader
even though he's a true alpha.

00:08:24.009 --> 00:08:29.099
That whole history speech about great leaders
failing greatly was foreshadowing for him.

00:08:29.099 --> 00:08:32.720
It's not a spoiler since Jeff Davis explained
the new character Liam.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.430
But he's going to be Scott's beta.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:40.860
I don't know how or why Scott will turn him,
but remember what the Calvares said.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.220
If he ever turned a person they'd come for
him too.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.500
So eventually they'll show up, for better
or worse.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.060
Hopefully they'll help with Kate while they're
around.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.279
Overall I thought the episode was a solid
B plus, it did an okay job of resolving the

00:08:53.279 --> 00:08:54.980
Derek plot even if the explanation defied
logic.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:09:01.100
And it did a good job of setting up the interpack
dynamics and plots going forward.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.900
Detective Banshee, Failed Leader made stronger
by the experience and the romantic 'ships.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:12.550
We still need to meet the new freshman lacrosse
players which I think is in episode 3.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.870
But in the meantime, I'll try to get a bonus
video out next Monday, be sure to subscribe

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.870
to get it.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:23.680
I think I'll either make it about the lore
of the Triskelion or feel free to suggest

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.040
some other aspect of Teen Wolf lore.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:30.230
Right now click here for my episode 1 review
and click here for my personal Q&amp;A I did during

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.230
VidCon.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.560
I answer all kinds of weird questions about
myself you guys asked me.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:33.560
It was fun.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:34.560
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:34.850
High Fives!

